   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">Ubuntu 12.04.5 LTS (GNU/Linux 3.13.0-39-generic x86_64)</p><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">$ sudo dpkg --purge RRO-8.0-Beta</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">dpkg: warning: there&#39;s no installed package matching RRO-8.0-Beta</p></div><div><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">$ sudo dpkg --purge RRO-8.0</p><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">dpkg: warning: there&#39;s no installed package matching RRO-8.0</p></div><div><br></div>Here is the install.sh in the downloaded package. Maybe it did not install the package correctly?<div><br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(52,187,199)\">#!/bin/bash</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(175,173,36)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>echo</b></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><b>&quot;Installing RRO-8.0-Beta&quot;</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">apt-get -y <span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>install</b></span> gcc<span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,165,0)\"> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">apt-get -y <span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>install</b></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>make</b></span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,165,0)\"> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">apt-get -y <span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>install</b></span> gfortran-4.8<span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,165,0)\"> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">apt-get -y <span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>install</b></span> liblzma-dev</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">dpkg -i RRO-8.0-Beta-Ubuntu-12.04.x86_64.deb 2<span style=\"color:rgb(52,189,38)\">&gt;</span>/dev/null 1<span style=\"color:rgb(52,189,38)\">&gt;</span>/dev/null</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(52,189,38)\">if<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(175,173,36)\"><b>&quot;$?&quot;</b></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span>-ne<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> 0 </span>];<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span>then<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(0,165,0)\"> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">apt-get -y <span style=\"color:rgb(52,189,38)\">-f</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(83,48,225)\"><b>install</b></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(52,189,38)\">fi</p><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Dec 12, 2014 at 11:15 AM, Joanne Contact <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">joanne...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Something is wrong. Since it is not usable, I am trying to remove it. But the uninstall does not find the package.<div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&#39;Menlo Regular&#39;;color:black\">$ls /usr/lib64/</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&#39;Menlo Bold&#39;;color:rgb(64,11,217)\">RRO-8.0</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&#39;Menlo Regular&#39;;color:black\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">$ sudo dpkg --purge RRO-8.0</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">dpkg: warning: there&#39;s no installed package matching RRO-8.0</p></div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
