     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">I found the package name is rro.</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">$ dpkg -S /usr/lib64/RRO-8.0/R-3.1.1/bin</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">rro: /usr/lib64/RRO-8.0/R-3.1.1/bin</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">$ sudo dpkg --purge rro</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">(Reading database ... 183586 files and directories currently installed.)</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">Removing rro ...</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">Purging configuration files for rro ...</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11px;font-family:Menlo\">dpkg: warning: while removing rro, directory &#39;/usr/lib64/RRO-8.0/R-3.1.1/lib/R/library&#39; not empty so not removed.</p><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Menlo;font-size:11px\"><a href=\"http://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/documents/rro/installation/#revorinst-li