     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Joanne,<div>This is the command to find out which RRO you have:<br></div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">dpkg -l | grep -i rro-</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div>Which will output something like this, depending on RRO version installed:</div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">ii  rro-8.0.1                       3.1.2-2</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>To remove:</div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">dpkg --purge rro-8.0.1</span></div></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"><br></span></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">hope this helps,</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Chris</font></div></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p><font size=\"4\"><a href=\"http://revolutionanalytics.com/plus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://revolutionanalytics.com/plus&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242027994000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2juwavcv0roasn_o0oHKN2\">Revolution R Plus</a></font></p><p><font size=\"4\">Subscribe to Technical Support &amp; Indemnification for R</font></p></div>"
